    "description": "Call pr-review v0.21.0 by its commit sha\n\n## Summary\n\nCrew's pull request review now runs on the latest release of pr-review, v0.21.0, in place of v0.5.0. The workflow calls that release by its full commit SHA, with the tag in a comment, so the reference cannot move. Nothing else in the workflow needed a change: the triggers, the permissions and the secret are the same in v0.21.0.\n\n**Ticket:** N/A\n**Type:** Refactor\n\n---\n\n## Agent context\n\n### Authority\n\n- `jerridan/pr-review` README, \"Set up CI\" at commit `047fb726fe4f7cb50984e2d973048fc90e677cf7` (tag `v0.21.0`): the consumer workflow, and the SHA-pin form `review.yml@<sha> # v<version>`.\n- `jerridan/pr-review` `.github/workflows/review.yml` at the same commit: the reusable workflow this file calls.\n- `CLAUDE.md`, \"Constraints that are easy to get wrong\": the version rule. A `.github/` file never reaches a plugin user, so this PR bumps no version.\n\n### What changed, by file\n\n- `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`: `uses:` calls `jerridan/pr-review/.github/workflows/review.yml@047fb726fe4f7cb50984e2d973048fc90e677cf7 # v0.21.0`, in place of `@v0.5.0`.\n\n### Constraints that applied\n\n- Change only what the new version needs. I compared the rest of the file with the two sources below, and nothing else differs.\n- No version bump: the change does not touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `hooks/` or the manifests.\n\n### How this was verified\n\n- `gh api repos/jerridan/pr-review/git/ref/tags/v0.21.0` gives the commit `047fb726fe4f7cb50984e2d973048fc90e677cf7`, and `gh api repos/jerridan/pr-review/releases/latest` gives `v0.21.0`.\n- Triggers: the README consumer workflow lists `pull_request` (opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review), `pull_request_target` (labeled) and `issue_comment` (created). This file lists the same three, with the same types.\n- Permissions: the README and the reusable workflow's job both ask for `pull-requests: write`, `checks: write` and `contents: write`. This file grants the same three.\n- Secrets: the reusable workflow reads one secret, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, and sets `GH_TOKEN` from the job token. This file passes `secrets: inherit`, and the repo holds `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`.\n- The reusable workflow file at `v0.5.0` and at `v0.21.0` is byte for byte the same (`diff` printed nothing). The changes between the two releases are in the action code that the workflow checks out at its own commit.\n- `grep -c 'uses: jerridan/pr-review/.github/workflows/review.yml@047fb726fe4f7cb50984e2d973048fc90e677cf7 # v0.21.0' .github/workflows/pr-review.yml` prints 1, and the diff names only that file.\n- The \"PR review\" check on this PR is the live test: it runs the new version.\n\n### Known gaps\n\n- The README example in pr-review still shows the tag `v0.2.0`. That is pr-review's file, not this repo's.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZgYWHHNhRSy3s6RFPj\n",
